<Plain
	title="About · today.duinlab.nl"
	description="What today.duinlab.nl is, what it keeps (nothing about you), where its facts come from, and its source code."
>
	<Fragment slot="title">About this page</Fragment>

	<p>
		A small daily paper for two people in The Hague, public for anyone who finds it: one picture, a few
		facts, a word, a quiz and ten daily games. It turns over at midnight, Amsterdam time.
	</p>

	<h2>Privacy</h2>
	<p>
		The page sets no cookies and runs no analytics. Played marks, streaks and quiz answers stay in your
		browser's local storage (keys <code>today.games.v1</code> and <code>today.quiz.v1</code>) and are never
		sent anywhere. Clear your site data to remove them.
	</p>
	<p>
		The page is served by a Cloudflare Worker. Cloudflare keeps request logs (the address requested, the time,
		and connection details such as your IP address) for a few days so problems can be traced. Nobody uses them
		for anything else.
	</p>

	<h2>Accessibility</h2>
	<p>
		The aim is WCAG 2.2 AA: text contrast checked against every sky, a 44-pixel target for every game and
		answer, keyboard focus you can see, motion that stops when your system asks for less, and a page that reads
		in full without JavaScript. Each change is checked with axe in the test suite. If something gets in your
		way, <a href="https://github.com/simonvanlierde/duinlab-today/issues">open an issue</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Sources</h2>
	<p>
		Every fact links to where it came from: Wikipedia (On this day, Did you know), Wiktionary (word of the day),
		NASA APOD and The Metropolitan Museum of Art (public-domain works), Open Trivia DB (CC BY-SA 4.0), ZenQuotes,
		and <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">Open-Meteo</a> for the weather. The weather line links to
		<a href="https://www.buienradar.nl/weer/den-haag/nl/2747373">Buienradar</a> for the full forecast and rain
		radar. The sky follows the sun over The Hague, worked out on the page; no API is asked.
	</p>

	<h2>Code</h2>
	<p>
		<a href="https://github.com/simonvanlierde/duinlab-today">github.com/simonvanlierde/duinlab-today</a>, MIT
		licence. The day's data is also at <a href="/today.json">today.json</a>.
	</p>
</Plain>
